---
id: org.dxos.plugin.presenter
name: PresenterPlugin
version: 0.1.0
---

A presentation plugin for DXOS Composer. A Presentation is an ordered deck of sections, each an owned markdown slide or a link to any workspace object, shown in the navtree as a folder of slides and presented with fullscreen mode and keyboard navigation. A markdown document can still be previewed as a deck through its Presenter companion.

## Extensions

The following extension dialects are used in this document.
Each extension is defined in the Appendix or resolved via its URI.

| Term        | URI                            |
|-------------|--------------------------------|
| `type`      | `org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0`       |
| `feat`      | `org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0`       |
| `scenario`  | `org.dxos.mdl.scenario@1.0`   |
| `component` | `org.dxos.mdl.component@1.0`  |
| `op`        | `org.dxos.mdl.op@1.1`         |
| `test`      | `org.dxos.mdl.test@1.0`       |
| `step`      | `org.dxos.mdl.step@1.0`       |
| `decision`  | `org.dxos.mdl.decision@1.0`   |

## Types

```mdl
type Presentation
  desc: |
    An ordered deck of sections. Typename `org.dxos.type.presentation@0.1.0`. A section is either an owned
    markdown `Text` (parented to the presentation) or a link to any other ECHO object, which keeps its own parent.
    Ownership is set explicitly when a slide is created, never by a schema annotation. Its navtree node lists
    `sections`; removing an owned slide there deletes its `Text`, removing a linked one only unlinks it.
  fields:
    name?: string
    sections: Ref<Obj>[]        # slide order; one section is exactly one slide
```

```mdl
type SlideViewState
  desc: |
    Per-user, per-deck view state (`presenter-slide`, local backend) in `@dxos/react-ui-attention`,
    keyed by the Presentation's (or previewed document's) URI. Never syncs to collaborators.
  fields:
    index: number               # zero-based index of the slide this user is viewing; clamped to the deck on read
```

```mdl
type SlideSource
  literals: markdown | object
  desc: |
    One resolved slide of a deck: `markdown` (owned Text, linked Markdown.Document or a preview section) carries
    content; `object` (any other linked object) carries a ref rendered through the slide surface fallback.
```

## Components

```mdl
component Deck
  desc: |
    Paged slide deck. Inline it shows a toolbar pager; in fullscreen an overlay pager that auto-hides when idle
    and wakes on pointer movement. Keys are scoped to the deck's focus scope, never `window`: left and right
    step, Shift+left and Shift+right (or Home and End) jump to first and last, `f` toggles fullscreen,
    Escape exits fullscreen.
  props:
    slides: SlideSource[]
    index: number
    fullscreen: boolean
    toolbar?: ReactNode
  actions:
    onIndexChange(index: number)
    onFullscreenChange(fullscreen: boolean)
    onAddSlide()
  layout: |
    ┌─────────────────────────────┐
    │ [toolbar]  ◀ 3 / 12 ▶  [⛶] │  ← hidden in fullscreen
    ├─────────────────────────────┤
    │                             │
    │     SlideFrame (slide N)    │
    │   (overlay pager, idle)     │
    └─────────────────────────────┘
```

```mdl
component PresentationArticle
  desc: |
    A Presentation's article is its deck. Fullscreen is read per object (is this Presentation on the
    fullscreen plank) and toggles in place on the Presentation's own plank; the current slide is per-viewer
    view state. The toolbar adds slides and links objects through SectionPicker.
  props:
    subject: Presentation
    attendableId?: string
```

```mdl
component SlideEditorArticle
  desc: Article for an owned slide: a markdown editor, opened by clicking the slide's child node in the navtree.
  props:
    subject: Text
```

```mdl
component SectionPicker
  desc: Toolbar picker over the space's objects that links the chosen object into the presentation as a section.
  props:
    presentation: Presentation
```

```mdl
component SlideFrame
  desc: |
    A fixed 16:9 logical canvas scaled to its container, so every slide contributor designs for one size.
    SlideRenderer wraps linked object slides in it; the markdown slide surface (SlideArticle) renders the
    slide only and relies on the caller for the frame.
  props:
    children: ReactNode
```

```mdl
component SlideRenderer
  desc: |
    Renders one SlideSource. Markdown sources render markdown; object sources render through the
    AppSurface.Slide surface, falling back to a title slide while no surface matches, and request gated slide
    surfaces on demand.
  props:
    source: SlideSource
```

```mdl
component DocumentArticle
  desc: |
    Presenter companion of a Markdown document: a Reveal.js player over the document content, split into slides
    on horizontal `---` separators. Vertical slides are not configured. Nothing is persisted. Fullscreen is read
    per object from the deck's fullscreen plank (is this document presented), not from the global layout mode.
    The companion stays on Reveal.js until the markdown renderer replaces it.
  props:
    document: Markdown.Document
  actions:
    exit()                      # exits fullscreen for this document
```

```mdl
component SlideArticle
  desc: |
    The AppSurface.Slide surface for Markdown.Document objects: renders the document as a slide, without a
    frame (SlideRenderer owns it).
  props:
    document: Markdown.Document
```

## Operations

```mdl
op TogglePresentation
  key: org.dxos.operation.presenter.setPresenting
  desc: |
    Enters or exits presentation for a Markdown document or Presentation by toggling the deck's
    fullscreen overlay (EphemeralDeckState.fullscreen). A Markdown document presents through its presenter
    companion node; a Presentation presents fullscreen on its own plank, since its article is the deck.
    The overlay is independent of what is open, so neither direction navigates: the URL and the
    open planks are unchanged.
  input:
    object: Markdown.Document | Presentation
    state: boolean              # on or off; callers that flip read the current state first
  output: void
  effects: [deck:fullscreen]
  requires: [DeckCapabilities.EphemeralState, DeckOperation.Adjust]
  note: |
    For a document the path is `<objectPath>/~presenter`; for a Presentation it is the plank's own path.
    Keyboard shortcut: Shift+Cmd+P (macOS), Shift+Alt+P (Windows/Linux).
```

## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: Presentation Mode

  req F-1.1: Every Markdown document in the workspace has a companion "Presenter" node in the app graph.
  req F-1.2:
    when: user activates TogglePresentation on a document
    then: the presenter companion fills the screen in the deck's fullscreen overlay, without the companion tab strip, and the URL does not change
  req F-1.3:
    when: user presses Shift+Cmd+P (macOS) or Shift+Alt+P (Windows)
    then: TogglePresentation is invoked for the focused object
  req F-1.4:
    when: user activates TogglePresentation on a Presentation
    then: the Presentation's own plank fills the screen in the fullscreen overlay and the URL does not change
```

```mdl
feat F-2: Document Preview (Reveal.js)

  req F-2.1:
    when: DocumentArticle mounts with a Markdown.Document
    then: RevealPlayer parses the document content and renders slides
  req F-2.2: Slides are separated by horizontal `---`; vertical slides are not configured.
  req F-2.3:
    when: user presses Escape or the exit action is triggered
    then: fullscreen exits for that document, leaving it and its companion as they were
```

```mdl
feat F-3: Presentation Object

  req F-3.1: A Presentation is created from the space's create-object menu and holds an ordered `sections` array.
  req F-3.2: One section is exactly one slide; `---` inside a section is a horizontal rule, not a slide break.
  req F-3.3: A section is an owned markdown Text (parented to the presentation) or a link to any object.
  req F-3.4:
    when: user adds a slide from the toolbar
    then: a new owned Text section is appended
  req F-3.5:
    when: user links an object through SectionPicker
    then: the object becomes a section and keeps its own parent
  req F-3.6:
    when: an owned slide is removed from the presentation
    then: its Text is deleted
  req F-3.7:
    when: a linked section is removed from the presentation
    then: only the link is removed; the object remains
  req F-3.8: Presentation deletion does not cascade to linked objects.
```

```mdl
feat F-4: Presentation Deck

  req F-4.1:
    when: PresentationArticle mounts
    then: the slide at the viewer's stored index is shown, clamped to the deck
  req F-4.2: The pager shows the current slide and total count; an empty deck shows none.
  req F-4.3: Keys bind to the deck's focus scope, never `window`.
  req F-4.4:
    when: user presses `f`
    then: the deck toggles fullscreen in place
  req F-4.5:
    when: the deck is fullscreen and the pointer is idle
    then: the overlay pager hides, and shows again on pointer movement
  req F-4.6:
    when: user presses Escape in fullscreen
    then: the deck exits fullscreen
  req F-4.7: The current slide index is per-user view state, kept across navigation and reloads, and never shared with collaborators.
  req F-4.8: Only an attended deck takes focus on mount.
  req F-4.9: A linked object with no slide surface renders as a title slide rather than failing.
```

```mdl
feat F-5: Navtree Folder

  req F-5.1: A Presentation node lists its sections as children.
  req F-5.2: An owned slide is labelled by its name, else its first markdown heading, else "Slide N".
  req F-5.3:
    when: user drags a child to a new position
    then: `sections` is reordered to match
  req F-5.4:
    when: user clicks a slide child
    then: the slide's own article opens (SlideEditorArticle for an owned slide)
  req F-5.5:
    when: user removes an owned slide from the navtree
    then: the action is labelled "Remove from presentation" and deletes the slide's Text
```

## Acceptance

```mdl
scenario T-1: Document presenter opens in fullscreen
  given: a Markdown document exists in the workspace
  when: user invokes TogglePresentation (keyboard or action menu)
  then:
    - the presenter companion fills the screen in the deck's fullscreen overlay
    - RevealPlayer is visible with at least one slide
    - the URL is unchanged
```

```mdl
scenario T-2: Document slides split on separators
  given: a Markdown document with three `---`-separated sections
  when: DocumentArticle renders the document
  then:
    - three slides are produced
    - arrow-key navigation advances and retreats between slides
```

```mdl
scenario T-3: Exit returns to document view
  given: DocumentArticle is open in fullscreen
  when: user presses Escape
  then: the fullscreen overlay closes, leaving the document and its companion as they were
```

```mdl
scenario T-4: Presentation renders one slide per section
  given: a Presentation with one owned slide and one linked Markdown document
  when: PresentationArticle mounts
  then:
    - slide 0 shows the owned slide
    - the pager shows count = 2
```

```mdl
scenario T-5: Slide advance
  given: PresentationArticle at slide 0 with a three-section Presentation
  when: user presses the right arrow
  then:
    - slide index advances to 1
    - the pager shows "2 / 3"
```

```mdl
scenario T-6: Slide index survives reload
  given: PresentationArticle at slide 1
  when: the app reloads and the Presentation is opened again
  then: slide 1 is shown
```

```mdl
scenario T-7: Keyboard shortcut registered
  given: a Markdown document node is focused in the app graph
  then:
    - action with key TogglePresentation is present on the node
    - keyBinding shows Shift+Cmd+P on macOS
```

```mdl
scenario T-8: Presentation presents fullscreen on its own plank
  given: a Presentation is open
  when: user presses `f`
  then:
    - the deck fills the screen with the overlay pager
    - Escape returns the deck to its plank
```

```mdl
scenario T-9: Reorder in the navtree
  given: a Presentation with three slides
  when: user drags the third slide to the top
  then: the deck order and the pager follow the navtree order
```

```mdl
scenario T-10: Removing a linked section keeps the object
  given: a Presentation with a linked Markdown document
  when: user removes the section
  then:
    - the section leaves the Presentation
    - the document still exists
```

