## QA

Executable tests. Each step carries a human instruction (`do`) and, where the step maps to an
invocable operation, an agent binding (`invoke`). Report failures by test and step number.

```mdl
test QA-1: Preview a document in the companion, then present it
  desc: The core presenter round-trip — create a document with slide separators, preview it in the presenter companion, present it fullscreen, then exit.
  actors: both
  covers: [F-1.1, F-1.2, F-2.1, F-2.2, F-2.3, T-1, T-3]
  status: unverified
  automated:
    - composer-e2e:presenter.spec.ts#Presenter › preview a document in the companion, then present it
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - space: a space is open
    - collection: a collection in that space, to create into
    - plugin-presenter is enabled — it is OFF by default (absent from `getDefaults` in
      `plugin-defs.tsx`), though the plugin itself is registered unconditionally so it always
      appears in the plugin registry to enable manually
    - no document named "QA Slides" exists — ABORT rather than deleting one this test did not create
  steps:
    - name: Create a document with slides
      do: In the navtree, click + on a collection and choose Markdown. Name it "QA Slides".
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.markdown.createDraft { name: "QA Slides", content: "# Slide one\n\n---\n\n# Slide two\n" }
      capture: created
      expect: a Document named "QA Slides" now exists with two `---`-separated sections
      assert: return !!$created.object
    - name: Place it
      do: (the navtree create action places it for you)
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.space.addObject { object: $created.object, target: $given.collection }
      expect: "QA Slides" appears as a row under the collection
    - name: Preview in the companion
      do: Open "QA Slides", open its companion and pick the Presenter tab.
      expect: the companion shows "Slide one" as a slide scaled to the companion's width
    - name: Enter presentation mode
      do: Choose Present from the document's actions menu, or press Shift+Cmd+P (macOS) / Shift+Alt+P (Windows/Linux).
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.presenter.setPresenting { object: $created.object, state: true }
      expect: the slides fill the screen showing "Slide one", with no companion tab strip; the URL is unchanged
      assert: return document.body.innerText.includes('Slide one');
    - name: Exit presentation mode
      do: Press Escape.
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.presenter.setPresenting { object: $created.object, state: false }
      expect: the document plank and its presenter companion are back as they were, and the URL is unchanged
      assert: return !!document.querySelector('[data-testid="deck.viewport"]');
  after:
    - name: Delete the document
      do: Right-click "QA Slides" in the navtree and choose Delete.
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.space.removeObjects { objects: [$created.object], target: $given.collection }
      expect: the row leaves the navtree and its plank closes

test QA-2: Showcase clip
  desc: |
    The 10s showcase clip: Present a document as slides and page through them. Recorded light at 60 fps with no ident, captions or
    count-in by `tools/autocue/showcase/overnight.mjs`; the clip is the `clip: presenter` step.
  actors: human
  status: unverified        # driven by autocue/showcase.mjs
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - space: a space is open
    - plugin-markdown, plugin-presenter enabled
  steps:
    - name: Present a document
      do: Write a document split by --- and press Shift+Cmd+P.
      expect: the first slide fills the plank
    - name: Page through
      do: Press the right arrow three times.
      expect: each slide shows in turn

test QA-3: Build and present a Presentation
  desc: Create a Presentation, add a slide, link a markdown document, reorder in the navtree, present it fullscreen, step, exit and reload.
  actors: human
  covers: [F-3.1, F-3.4, F-3.5, F-4.1, F-4.4, F-4.6, F-4.7, F-5.1, F-5.3, T-4, T-5, T-6, T-8, T-9]
  status: unverified
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - space: a space is open
    - plugin-markdown, plugin-presenter enabled
  steps:
    - name: Create a Presentation
      do: In the space's create-object menu choose Presentation and name it "QA Deck".
      expect: "QA Deck" appears in the navtree as a folder with no children
    - name: Add a slide
      do: Open "QA Deck" and click the add-slide button.
      expect: a child "New slide" appears and the pager shows "1 / 1"
    - name: Link a document
      do: Use the link-object picker to link an existing markdown document.
      expect: the document appears as a second child and the pager shows "1 / 2"
    - name: Reorder
      do: Drag the second child above the first in the navtree.
      expect: the order of the children and of the deck follows the drag
    - name: Present
      do: Press `f`, then step with the arrow keys.
      expect: the deck fills the screen, the overlay pager shows and hides with pointer movement, and each arrow press changes the slide
    - name: Exit and reload
      do: Press Escape, then reload the app and reopen "QA Deck".
      expect: the deck is inline again and shows the slide that was current before the reload
```

## Changelog

```mdl
decision D-1: A dedicated `Presentation` object owns an ordered list of sections, each an owned markdown `Text` or a link to any object, and is shown in the navtree as a folder of slides.
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [Presentation, F-3, F-5]
  source: docs/DESIGN.md Q1
```

```mdl
decision D-2: One section is exactly one slide.
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-3.2]
  source: docs/DESIGN.md Q2
```

```mdl
decision D-3: The markdown document companion stays as a quick preview split on `---`.
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [DocumentArticle, F-2]
  source: docs/DESIGN.md Q2b
```

```mdl
decision D-4: An object without a slide surface still renders through a fallback chain ending in a title slide; the picker toggle filters to objects with a dedicated slide surface.
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [SlideRenderer, F-4.9]
  source: docs/DESIGN.md Q3
```

```mdl
decision D-5: The current slide index is per-user, per-deck view state in `react-ui-attention` with the local backend.
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [SlideViewState, F-4.7]
  source: docs/DESIGN.md Q4
```

```mdl
decision D-6: The pager is a separate `Pager` primitive; `Carousel` shares its styles.
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [Deck]
  source: docs/DESIGN.md Q5
```

```mdl
decision D-7: The assistant skill is annotated on `Presentation` only and `agentCanEnable`.
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [Presentation]
  source: docs/DESIGN.md Q6
```

```mdl
decision D-8: A presenter view is deferred to a later phase; speaker notes are parsed now.
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [Deck]
  source: docs/DESIGN.md Q7
```

```mdl
decision D-9: Slide syntax is a strict Slidev-compatible subset rendered by the plugin's own pipeline.
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-2]
  source: docs/DESIGN.md Q8
```

```mdl
decision D-10: Collection decks, the `presentCollections` setting and the Settings module are removed; a Presentation replaces them. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [Presentation, F-1, F-3]
  why: A first-class deck object makes the experimental collection mode redundant.
  rejected: Keeping collection decks behind the setting.
```

```mdl
decision D-11: Owned slides are parented to the presentation explicitly when created, not by a schema annotation. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [Presentation, F-3.8]
  why: A parent annotation would also adopt linked parentless objects, so deleting a Presentation could delete them.
  rejected: `Annotation.SetParent` on `sections`.
```

```mdl
decision D-12: A Presentation presents fullscreen on its own plank. Fills in [D-4].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [TogglePresentation, F-1.4, T-8]
  why: A Presentation has no presenter companion; its article is the deck.
  rejected: Giving Presentation a presenter companion.
```

```mdl
decision D-13: Fullscreen state is read per object, so a fullscreen change for one deck does not remount or refocus another. Fills in [D-12].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [PresentationArticle, DocumentArticle]
  why: The global layout mode changes for every deck when any one toggles.
  rejected: Reading the global layout mode.
```

```mdl
decision D-14: Clicking a slide child in the navtree opens that slide's own article, the markdown editor for an owned slide. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-5.4, SlideEditorArticle]
  why: Slides need an editing surface, and the navtree is where a slide is selected.
  rejected: Opening the presentation at that slide.
```

```mdl
decision D-15: An owned slide's navtree label is its name, else its first heading, else "Slide N". Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-5.2]
  why: The Text type carries a name field that a person sets deliberately, so it takes precedence.
```

```mdl
decision D-16: Removing an owned slide from the navtree is labelled "Remove from presentation". Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-5.5]
  why: The generic label "Remove from collection" misdescribes a delete of the owned Text.
```

